# Ignore generated media files — regenerate with scripts/generate-test-corpus.cs
files/

# Subtitle sources. `subs/*` and not `subs/`, because git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded — the negation below is silently
# inert under a directory exclude, and `git add` drops the file.
#
# That distinction is invisible in this repository, where test-subtitles.srt is
# already tracked and the ignore therefore never applies to it. It becomes
# visible the moment a tree is rebuilt from `git archive` into a fresh repo:
# `git add -A` then honours the ignore and quietly leaves the file behind.
#
# generate-test-corpus.cs reads it (`if (File.Exists(srtPath))`) to produce
# test-with-subtitles.mkv, and skips that fixture without complaint when it is
# missing — so the loss shows up as subtitle tests skipping, not as an error.
subs/*
!subs/test-subtitles.srt

# Track metadata and scripts
!manifest.json
!.gitignore
